      "size": [
        400,
        420
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 22,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653",
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Trying number forms\n\nNode 8 is the whole experiment: type a number, pick what it is made of. Node 9's seed is **fixed** on purpose — change it deliberately and you can get a hand back that you liked.\n\nJudge on node 10's report, not on node 24. It says what fraction of the crop changed; over 8% means the model repainted the paper as well as writing on it, which looks fine in the preview and arrives on the sheet as a rectangle of somebody else's paper.\n\n**The reference carries a 1 and a 0.** Any other digit is the model transferring a manner, not copying a shape — that is the interesting case and also the one that fails. If a hand will not come out, 10, 13 or 31 sit in the frame exactly the same way.\n\n### Before the first run\n\n**Node 1 is the signature page**, `GIoS_Wehrmacht_Signed_Ru.jpg` (1860×2560). Not p1 — that one is 1024×1410, and at 4× it makes a 4096×5640 sheet the page directive knows nothing about. p1 belongs in node 6, where it is the reference for the hand. Node 2's report prints the size the plate will come out at; it is the cheapest place to catch this.\n\n**Node 3:** `gaussblur_radius` = **3**, not its default 8. Node 2 has already grown the mask by 3 px; past ~12 px total the halo of one typed line meets the next and a paragraph becomes one hole.\n\n**Memory.** Past node 5 every IMAGE is 7440×10240 — about 900 MB of float32 each, and the typing holds three or four at once.\n\n**Nothing is resampled.** Remacri runs at its trained 4×, and the number it lands on is what the `page` directive names."
      ]
    }
